Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:36:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: add the Xiaomi Marble M16T 36 0d 0b panel

Integrate the driver, cached backlight updates and bootloader power handoff.

Source changes (original messages and trailers follow).

Source-commit: 6b0581eb2527adf46e0fb020d30f7cbd7d771302
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-24T10:36:59+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0047-drm-panel-add-the-Xiaomi-marble-M16T-36-0d-0b-panel.patch

drm/panel: add the Xiaomi marble M16T 36 0d 0b panel

Marble ships with at least two M16T DSC video-mode panels. ABL names
the fitted one in msm_drm.dsi_display0; the existing driver
(xiaomi,marble-m16t-36-02-0a) covers "36 02 0a", while this phone has
qcom,mdss_dsi_m16t_36_0d_0b_dsc_vid ("xiaomi 36 0d 0b video mode dsc
dsi panel", mi,panel-id <0x4d313654 0x360201>), which stays black with
the 02 0a sequence.

The 0d 0b panel uses a different controller command set: a different
on/off sequence, reset sequence, vertical porches (fp 16, pw 4,
bp 12), supply order (vddio, vci, vddd) and a vddd of 1.25 V instead
of 1.2 V. Add a separate driver rather than a variant
table in the 02 0a driver, which is built around a Novatek register
set and DSC RC table that do not apply here.

The driver was generated with linux-mdss-dsi-panel-driver-generator
(https://github.com/msm8916-mainline/linux-mdss-dsi-panel-driver-generator,
28c4df2, --dumb-dcs) from the device tree of the stock Android
running on the phone, then adapted:

- reset: a full high-low-high pulse (high 11 ms, low 1 ms, high
  11 ms; the stock 36 02 0a qcom,mdss-dsi-reset-sequence <1 11>,
  <0 1>, <1 11>) instead of this panel's stock <0 1>, <1 20>. The
  downstream pairs are raw GPIO levels; with the active-low
  reset-gpios the generated code mapped them correctly (assert 1 ms,
  release 20 ms). Since the reset is already asserted at that point,
  that sequence is a single release, and on hardware the panel then
  ignores all DCS reads (power mode read fails with -ENODATA, black
  screen). With the high-low-high pulse it reports power mode 0x9c
  and ID c2 b6 32 and displays;
- compatible "xiaomi,marble-m16t-36-0d-0b", explicit stock supply
  order and delays, MIPI_DSI_MODE_DSC_ALL_SLICES_IN_PKT for
  qcom,mdss-dsc-slice-per-pkt = <2> and RGB888 as in the 02 0a driver;
- stock qcom,mdss-dsc-config-by-manufacture-cmd: the decoder PPS is
  sent as manufacturer command 0x70 in the on sequence. It describes
  DSC 1.1, 10 bpc, 8 bpp, 540x12 slices (stock DT says slice height
  20, but the PPS fields are derived from 12). The DSC config uses
  these values and explicit RC parameters, so drm/msm keeps them and
  drm_dsc_compute_rc_parameters() reproduces the 0x70 bytes; the
  standard PPS is sent as well with identical contents.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Source-commit: 85e13f37392e07feedb83ef35a0e7f91b9d8a47e
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-24T17:15:32+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0048-drm-panel-xiaomi-m16t-36-0d-0b-skip-backlight-update.patch

drm/panel: xiaomi-m16t-36-0d-0b: skip backlight updates while unprepared

drm/msm's DSI host rejects every transfer while its link is off
(dsi_host_transfer() returns -EINVAL without power_on), so a sysfs
brightness write while the panel is blanked fails with EINVAL. On an
installed system, systemd-backlight restores the level at boot and
failed five times in a row ("Failed to write system 'brightness'
attribute: Invalid argument") while fb0 was blanked.

Do as upstream commit 3367c5a129f7 ("drm/panel: sofef00: Fix DSI
transfer errors on backlight update") does: return early while the
panel is not prepared. The backlight core keeps the level in
bl->props.brightness, and drm_panel_enable() sends it through
backlight_enable() at the next power-on. Also restore the LPM mode
flag when the DCS write fails, so a failed update does not leave
later commands in high-speed mode.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Source-commit: cdf94e9270dbd36b6adc51576db4b848417f3eba
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-24T20:54:21+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0050-drm-panel-xiaomi-m16t-36-0d-0b-power-the-panel-down-.patch

drm/panel: xiaomi-m16t-36-0d-0b: power the panel down at probe

On Marble the first bring-up after boot leaves the panel black: the on
sequence, PPS and compression mode commands all succeed, but every DCS
read fails (power mode read returns -ENODATA, ID reads zeros). After a
DPMS cycle the same prepare works (power mode 0x9c, ID c2 b6 32).

Keeping the display PLL that ABL left running (previous commit) removes
the "disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src: rcg didn't update its configuration"
warning, but on its own the panel still stays black at boot. The
power-down alone, without the PLL fix, did not help either. With both, a
build that additionally traced DCS readbacks in prepare and enable lit
the panel from boot.

ABL leaves the panel powered (continuous splash). The supplies are RPMh
LDOs; the first regulator_enable() only adds the APPS vote to rails that
are already on. In the working DPMS cycle the supplies really turn off
(unprepare releases the last reference, the RPMh disable from the APPS
DRV replaces ABL's vote) and the DSI host and PHY are powered down right
after, so the panel sits unpowered for about 300 ms with idle lanes.

A power-down at the start of the first prepare (100 ms, later 500 ms
with the rails verified off) did not help: by then the DSI host has
already powered the PHY and drives LP-11 into the unpowered panel.

Power the panel down in probe, before attaching to the DSI host: with
reset asserted, take each supply and release it in the stock off order,
then keep it off for 500 ms. The DSI host is brought up only after the
panel has attached, so the lanes are idle during that time. Prepare is
unchanged. This delays the first display bring-up by half a second.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
